WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:00.644
Hey.

00:00:00.644 --> 00:00:03.736
I'm Soya, a cat who explains things.

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:06.656
Today: what is a software factory?

00:00:06.656 --> 00:00:07.601
One minute.

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:08.374
Let's go.

00:00:09.024 --> 00:00:14.262
A factory makes the same thing again and again, in steps you can check.

00:00:14.262 --> 00:00:16.697
Cookies: dough, bake, check, box.

00:00:16.697 --> 00:00:18.910
Apps: idea, build, check, app.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.981
Ours has five steps.

00:00:20.981 --> 00:00:22.899
One: read what's new in AI.

00:00:22.899 --> 00:00:26.381
Two: pick the idea that helps a real person most.

00:00:27.031 --> 00:00:28.843
Three: build one tiny app.

00:00:28.843 --> 00:00:29.889
Four: check it.

00:00:29.889 --> 00:00:33.793
Tests, a scan for secrets, and a look at a phone screen.

00:00:34.443 --> 00:00:35.711
Five: ask a human.

00:00:35.711 --> 00:00:40.572
The factory sends a request that says: here's my change, take a look.

00:00:40.572 --> 00:00:42.192
No skipping the checks.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.225
The trend right now?

00:00:44.225 --> 00:00:45.954
An agent above the tools.

00:00:45.954 --> 00:00:49.687
It decides what's next, checks the result, follows up.

00:00:49.687 --> 00:00:51.554
Some call it an outer loop.

00:00:51.554 --> 00:00:52.867
We run a small one.

00:00:53.517 --> 00:00:56.253
But an agent is only as good as its rules.

00:00:56.253 --> 00:01:00.749
Ours can't spend money, can't open accounts, can't promise ownership.

00:01:00.749 --> 00:01:01.986
Humans decide that.

00:01:02.636 --> 00:01:03.725
Why tiny apps?

00:01:03.725 --> 00:01:06.914
Tiny things get finished, checked, fixed.

00:01:06.914 --> 00:01:10.258
So: one app a day, until something catches.

00:01:10.908 --> 00:01:11.751
I'm Soya.

00:01:11.751 --> 00:01:12.969
Try the apps.

00:01:12.969 --> 00:01:15.123
Tell us what you'd add.

00:01:15.123 --> 00:01:15.685
Later.

